interlocutor typically measured in terms of the cognitive cost of acquiring,
understanding, or producing a given language feature. Cognitive cost can be
influenced by language interference, or errors arising from the learning process, or
by the extent of an interlocutor’s exposure to a language feature. Therefore,
difficulty can intersect with complexity, but need not.
