adjectival form nor the demonymic form of countries’ and nations’ name. “Gaelscoilis” is a
term used to refer to incomplete acquisition of Irish that is reportedly spoken in some Irish
speaking schools. The term is pejorative, but is not been precisely defined, and the
sociolinguistic motivations for the phenomenon have not been investigated. The following is
