Reference documents for mainstream education describe the language learning process in
broadly similar terms to the CEFR (Council of Europe (2001)), the reference documents also
use relatively uniform structures and terminology throughout when prescribing language
features for each of their respective levels of ability. Figure 2 was created to show the
similarities between the terms and structures used in reference documents, and the way
